<title>JAPAN: Banker says seems BOJ not ready to lift rates-Jiji.</title>
<headline>Banker says seems BOJ not ready to lift rates-Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the Federation of Bankers Associations of Japan told a parliamentary committee meeting on Friday that he did not think the Bank of Japan (BOJ) was ready to raise interest rates, Jiji news agency said.</p>
<p>&quot;I understand that there are many who are suffering under ultra-low interest rates. But it seems that the BOJ does not think the situation calls for raising interest rates, judging from economic conditions,&quot; Naotaka Saeki was quoted as saying.</p>
</text>
